# React components

- One React component per file. A second component, even a "private" helper, goes to its own folder — do not wave it through as an internal helper.
- Component = folder with an index file; import via path aliases, never `../../../`.
- State placement: server state → the data layer ({{dataLayer}}); cross-cutting client state → the global store; everything else stays local.
- No business logic in JSX. Components render; hooks and the data layer decide.
- Styling: use the project theme / tokens. No hard-coded colour literals in UI code; a new token is added to the theme (light **and** dark if the app has both).
- Lists that can exceed ~100 items are virtualised.
- Every new component with logic gets a test next to it, asserting behaviour (text, roles, events) — not implementation details.
